#! beatscript 2
#! skip-test: binds seeds of the generator (gen@1), which tests/examples_beatscript.rs checks without; tested in crates/beatscript-api/tests/forms_roles.rs
#! name: cross two seeds
# cross-two-seeds.beatscript: two seeds of the generator, a dubstep one and a house one, crossed in the cross form (CC0). Original.
# The form gives the structure and the seeds fill its roles: `a=` and `b=` each give the melody, bass and chords of their drop,
# generated in this program's key and at its tempo, so the two cross without a clash though their own keys differ.
# What you hear: a leads, then b, then the two at once, b's tune over a's bass with a's tune under it as an arp; the morphs
# pull a toward b and back, a little more on every pass, and the phrase ("deep calleth unto deep") is sung over the crossing.
tempo 126
key am

arrange from template(cross, @psalm42_deep_calleth, a=gen@1 dubstep seed=54876, b=gen@1 house seed=7)
